s, making it better suitable for machine learning workflows.\n\n# Feature Engineering: Normalize Total Horizontal Distance\nscaler = MinMaxScaler()\ndf['Normalized_Total_Distance'] = scaler.fit_transform(df[['Total_horizontal_distance_features']])\n# Description: Normalizes total proximity distances using Min-Max scaling.\n# Usefulness: Keeps proximity features consistent and scale-agnostic for easier interpretation by models.\n\n# Feature Engineering: Bin Hydrology Distance Ratio\ndef bin_hydrology_ratio(value):\n    if value < 5:\n        return 'low'\n    elif value < 10:\n        return 'medium'\n    else:\n        return 'high'\n\ndf['Hydrology_Ratio_Bin'] = df['Hydrology_distance_ratio'].apply(bin_hydrology_ratio)\n# Description: Bins Hydrology Distance Ratio into categories.\n# Usefulness: Simplifies complex continuous distance values into directional categorical ranges for clearer trends.\n\n# Feature Engineering: Quadrant Encoding for Aspect\none_hot_aspect = pd.get_dummies(df['Aspect_range_bin'], prefix='Aspect')\ndf = pd.concat([df, one_hot_aspect], axis=1)\n# Description: Transforms Aspect directionality into one-hot encoded quadrants.\n# Usefulness: Captures categorical terrain directionality, removing unnecessary model bias and retaining interpretability.", "df.drop(columns=['Soil_Type_sum', 'Wilderness_Areas_sum'], inplace=True)\n# Description: Soil_Type_sum and Wilderness_Areas_sum provide no additional predictive power as they are constant.\n# Usefulness: Reduces data redundancy for cleaner feature set.\n\ndf.drop(columns=['Fire_and_Road_Interaction'], inplace=True)\n# Description: Fire_and_Road_Interaction has an undefined mean and standard deviation due to presence of infinite values.\n# Usefulness: Prevents skewness issues and potential instability during modeling.\n\ndf.drop(columns=['Hydrology_and_Elevation_Interaction', 'Hydrology_distance_ratio'], inplace=True)\n# Description: Original interaction and ratio features have challenging skewness 